              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For truck drivers and fleet owners, the engine is the lifeblood of every route. When semi truck engine problems arise, the costs aren't just mechanical; they ripple into downtime, lost deliveries, and frustrated customers.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "stats-intro-1",
                  "type": "statBand",
                  "props": {
                    "stats": [
                      {
                        "value": "$2.270/mile",
                        "label": "Average repair and maintenance cost per mile in 2023, per the American Transportation Research Institute"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we've seen firsthand how catching issues early saves Florida fleets thousands. Here are the most common engine problems drivers should never ignore, and how to handle them before they escalate.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-common-problems",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Semi Truck Engine Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "common-problems"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "details-common-problems-1",
                  "type": "detail-cards",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stacked",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Overheating Engines",
                        "body": "Overheating is one of the most frequent and costly engine problems in Florida, where high heat and heavy hauls push cooling systems to their limit. Worn belts, low coolant, or radiator leaks are often to blame.",
                        "notes": [
                          {
                            "label": "WARNING SIGNS",
                            "text": "Rising temperature gauge, steam from under the hood, loss of power."
                          },
                          {
                            "label": "PREVENTION",
                            "text": "Schedule cooling system inspections and replace hoses and belts before they fail."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Fuel System Failures",
                        "body": "Clogged filters, injector malfunctions, or contaminated fuel can cause reduced power and efficiency. Left unchecked, these issues can result in breakdowns or even catastrophic engine failure.",
                        "notes": [
                          {
                            "label": "WARNING SIGNS",
                            "text": "Hard starts or stalling, rough idling, drop in fuel economy."
                          },
                          {
                            "label": "PREVENTION",
                            "text": "Stick to fuel filter replacement schedules and monitor for contamination."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Oil Leaks and Lubrication Issues",
                        "body": "Engine lubrication keeps internal parts running smoothly. Oil leaks not only create environmental hazards but also lead to accelerated wear and eventual breakdowns.",
                        "notes": [
                          {
                            "label": "WARNING SIGNS",
                            "text": "Oil puddles under the truck, low oil pressure readings, smoke from the exhaust."
                          },
                          {
                            "label": "PREVENTION",
                            "text": "Regularly check seals, gaskets, and filters. Never delay oil changes."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Turbocharger Failures",
                        "body": "Turbochargers boost power and efficiency but operate under extreme pressure and heat. Failure often results from oil contamination or poor maintenance.",
                        "notes": [
                          {
                            "label": "WARNING SIGNS",
                            "text": "Loss of acceleration, excessive exhaust smoke, whining or grinding noises."
                          },
                          {
                            "label": "PREVENTION",
                            "text": "Use high-quality oil and maintain proper lubrication intervals."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Electrical and Sensor Malfunctions",
                        "body": "Today's engines depend on complex electronics to regulate performance. Failing sensors can throw off the entire system, leading to reduced fuel efficiency and compliance issues.",
                        "notes": [
                          {
                            "label": "WARNING SIGNS",
                            "text": "Check engine light, erratic power delivery, failed emissions tests."
                          },
                          {
                            "label": "PREVENTION",
                            "text": "Diagnostics during preventive maintenance can catch issues before they leave you stranded."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-repair-vs-replace",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Repair Versus Replacement: Knowing The Difference",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "repair-vs-replace"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-repair-vs-replace-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not every engine issue requires a full replacement. A simple repair, such as replacing a fuel injector or gasket, may be enough to restore performance. But if failures are chronic or multiple systems are affected, a rebuild or overhaul becomes the smarter choice. Fleet managers should weigh:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-repair-vs-replace-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Cost per mile: Repeated small repairs can exceed the price of a replacement"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Downtime impact: A rebuild may take longer but reduce long-term breakdowns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Truck lifecycle: Older units may justify full replacement, while newer trucks benefit from targeted repairs"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-repair-vs-replace-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Experiencing engine issues? Don't let unscheduled downtime keep you off the road. Schedule an appointment with our service team at Sun State International. We'll help get back on track ASAP.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-repair-vs-replace-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-repair-vs-replace-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
